+// The stand-ins for the audio and movie decoders the Linux build does not have yet.
+//
+// hle_audio.c and hle_movie*.c run on Apple's AudioToolbox and VideoToolbox. On Linux
+// they need a device layer (ALSA / PulseAudio for the output, dav1d for AV1) that is not
+// written, so the service entries they provide are missing until it is: the loader's
+// unimplemented stubs cover the imports, and the functions the rest of the host calls
+// directly are answered here with the smallest thing that keeps the host running.
+//
+//   dm_audio_suspend / dm_pcmout_*  the audio service: one silent PCM output which never
+//                                    produces samples (dm_audio_suspend releases it)
+//   mavc_* / mav1_* / md_nv12 / md_rgba  the movie decoders: every decoder fails to
+//                                    initialize, which the SDK's movie module reports as
+//                                    it does on a device with no decoder
+//   mtl_pso_prebuild_tool            the offline pipeline prebuild: nothing to prebuild
